%% Request / ingest sequence — attacker probe → honeypot → relay → Postgres + Redis → Grafana
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Attacker as Attacker
    participant DNS as Cloudflare DNS
    participant CAD as gateway (Caddy)
    participant HP as honeypot (Java)
    participant VOL as honeypot-data (vol)
    participant RLY as relay (Python)
    participant PG as postgres (TimescaleDB)
    participant RDS as redis (Streams)
    participant PR as prometheus
    participant GR as grafana
    participant AM as alertmanager

    Attacker->>DNS: resolve honeypot.example.com
    DNS-->>Attacker: <public IP>
    Attacker->>CAD: TCP 443, ClientHello
    CAD->>CAD: TLS handshake (Cloudflare DNS-01 cert)
    Attacker->>CAD: SSH banner "SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_8.9"
    CAD->>HP: reverse-proxy  → honeypot:2222
    HP-->>CAD: fake banner "SSH-2.0-Honeypot"
    CAD-->>Attacker: relay banner
    Attacker->>HP: brute-force attempts (user/pass)
    HP->>HP: log4j JSON  →  /data/honeypot.log
    HP->>HP: SQLite INSERT INTO auth_attempts
    HP-->>CAD: shell prompt (low-interaction)
    CAD-->>Attacker: shell prompt
    Attacker->>HP: session commands
    HP->>HP: INSERT INTO commands, sessions

    loop every 10s (poll) / on FS event (watchdog)
        RLY->>VOL: read /data/honeypot.db (SQLite WAL)
        RLY->>VOL: read /data/honeypot.log (tail)
        RLY->>PG: INSERT INTO events.attack (... returning id)
        RLY->>RDS: XADD honeynet:events:attack * data {...}
    end

    PR->>RLY: GET /metrics  (every 15s)
    RLY-->>PR: relay_events_shipped_total{source="db"} 42
    PR->>PR: rule "AttackSurge" evaluation
    PR-->>AM: alert escalated (critical, security)
    AM-->>PagerDuty: Events API v2
    AM-->>Slack: webhook post

    GR->>PG: SELECT count(*), date_trunc('minute', ts) ...
    GR->>RDS: XLEN honeynet:events:attack
    GR-->>Attacker: ◀ dashboard renders for the analyst only